                    {
                        "sense_id": "220cb223-d7bf-3d16-9182-c8fba5a78b75",
                        "entry_id": "09de2f91-9765-3dae-9a36-b8090b1831b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of celemin, a traditional Spanish unit of dry measure equivalent to about 4.6 liters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6020e4e-37d0-4923-8696-cbfd9569e235",
                                "sense_id": "220cb223-d7bf-3d16-9182-c8fba5a78b75",
                                "text": "An almud is a measure of volume rather than weight; an almud of wheat equals about 22 pounds and an almud of potatoes 20 pounds."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1f462da1-b0e2-4cca-b9e8-e34a6f60e455",
                                "sense_id": "220cb223-d7bf-3d16-9182-c8fba5a78b75",
                                "text": "Both sexes were equally familiar with and preferred the Spanish almud (equal to four quarts of seed), often rendered almo in Nahuatl, over any indigenous measure."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a1bd8b14-db14-3409-86a2-bc1f749c5478",
                        "entry_id": "09de2f91-9765-3dae-9a36-b8090b1831b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A traditional Spanish unit of dry measure, highly variable depending on the location and the substance measured but generally between 3 and 20 liters."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "444bdf38-00c6-325b-b2b8-eb7d768229b1",
                        "entry_id": "09de2f91-9765-3dae-9a36-b8090b1831b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A traditional Spanish unit of land area (nominally, the area cultivable by an almud of some particular seed), highly variable depending on the location."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f2f9d6f9-0100-3fc9-9e93-559768bbe282",
                        "entry_id": "09de2f91-9765-3dae-9a36-b8090b1831b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A low wide box once used for measuring almuds."
                        ],
